Still pending (headless getDisplayMedia probably hangs waiting). Status stays "Escolha...". It may remain pending indefinitely in headless. Not a problem in real browsers, but the promise never settles in headless. No errors.

But if the user cancels the picker, it rejects → handled.

One issue: if a second start is attempted while pending, we could get double. Guard with a `this.prismPending` flag. Add:
```js
if (this.prismPending) return;
this.prismPending = true;
try {...} finally { this.prismPending = false; }
```
And disable the start button while pending? UI set status enough.

Also stopPrismCapture while getDisplayMedia pending should cancel? Can't cancel the picker; if it resolves later, attach would activate. Edge case; guard: capture a token. Let's add a simple `_prismRequest` counter: increment on start; stop sets `this.prismRequest = 0`? Overkill. But a user clicking CAPTURAR then PARAR before picking would end up streaming after selection. Add:

```js
async startPrismCapture() {
  if (this.prismPending) return;
  this.prismPending = true;
  const request = (this.prismToken = (this.prismToken || 0) + 1);
  ...
  try { await feed.start(...) } catch {... return} finally { this.prismPending=false }
  if (request !== this.prismToken) { feed.stop(); return; }
  ...
}
stopPrismCapture() { this.prismToken = (this.prismToken||0)+1; ... }
```

Handle in finally carefully: return inside catch still runs finally. Fine.

Also, since the test left a pending getDisplayMedia promise, reloading the page clears it.

Additionally, there's another subtlety: `startPrismCapture` calls `feed.start` while capture may already be active; `attach` detaches old. Fine.

Another important point: mobile/Safari support for getDisplayMedia is absent → setPrismStamp disables the button and shows status. But `btn-prism` and menu button still open the panel; that's fine.

Now update the pending guard, then final build and test with a fresh page.

Also should the `P` key open the panel during "boot"? Currently togglePrism returns early if mode === "boot", but mode is "menu" while the boot screen is visible (constructor opens menu). So pressing P on the boot screen opens the panel behind the boot overlay. Minor. We can gate by `document.getElementById("boot").classList.contains("hidden")`. Better in togglePrism:

```js
togglePrism(show) {
  if (this.mode === "boot" || !document.getElementById("boot")?.classList.contains("hidden")) return;
  ...
}
```
Hmm, when boot screen is visible, mode is menu anyway. Add check on boot visibility.

Also opening the panel from the menu covers the menu; okay.

