    treePosition: new THREE.Vector3(startFrame.x, 2.4, startFrame.z),
    raceLine: { profiles: profile, states: lineState, ds },
  };
  return api;
}

content.text:
Issue: `strip` is used before definition? Function declarations hoisted, so `curbMesh` is a function declaration inside buildTrack — hoisted too. `strip` is function declaration, hoisted. OK.

But `curbMesh` is declared after use in the loop; function declarations hoist, fine.

Another issue: `getSpacedPoints(N)` might return N+1 points. N is based on total/2. ds = total/N but getSpacedPoints spacing is total/N. Good.

Now physics.js changes: add curvature, braking, wall crash. Let me edit carefully.

Also need `jerk` / crash state. Add in reset:
```
this.wallTimer = 0;
this.wallHit = 0;
this.crashes = 0;
```
In step, replace lateral block. Also brake deceleration currently `this.brake*mass*11` and resistance; good. But when speed < 0.2 brake ignored. Fine.

Add curvature handling after speed integration:
```
this.wallTimer = max(0, this.wallTimer-dt)
const kappa = input.curvature || 0;
if (this.speed > 2 && !locked) {
  const latMax = s.grip * G * 0.95;
  const req = this.speed*this.speed*Math.abs(kappa);
  if (req > latMax) {
    const excess = req-latMax;
    this.lateralV -= Math.sign(kappa)*excess*0.62*dt;
    this.speed = Math.max(0, this.speed - excess*0.055*dt);
    this.slide = clamp((excess)/latMax,0,1);
  } else this.slide = Math.max(0, this.slide - dt*2);
  this.lateralV += this.steer * this.speed * 0.16 * dt;
}
```
Wait sign: for right curve (kappa>0), outward is left = negative lateral. lateralV -= sign(kappa)*... correct.

But the car following the path doesn't need lateral velocity; if target speed is adhered, no sliding. Good.

Need `slide` property init.

Also lateral recentering force? When on a curve, the path's lateral coordinate is in the car's moving frame; the centrifugal effect slides it outward. Fine.

Steer effect: with lane assist? We want the player to steer to stay on line but the car follows path automatically so no need. Steering also should produce a yaw visual (game adds steer yaw).

Wall:
```
const limit = 3.35;
if (Math.abs(this.lateral) > limit) {
  const sign = Math.sign(this.lateral);
  const impact = Math.min(1, Math.abs(this.lateralV) + this.speed*0.02);
  this.lateral = sign*limit;
  this.lateralV *= -0.22;
  if (this.wallTimer <= 0) { this.speed *= 0.80; this.wallTimer = 0.55; this.crashes++; this.hitWall = true; }
  else { this.speed *= Math.max(0, 1 - dt*1.4); }
}
```
Hmm hitWall only true on the initial impact; game can detect with justShifted? For toast, use `sim.hitWall`; new crash flag. Set `this.crashed = false` each step, `this.crashed = true` on impact. Game checks.

Clamp LATERAL limit maybe depends on course half width. Use input.lateralLimit || 3.4.

Also the sim must brake into curves based on player's action. Player is responsible for hitting brake. But auto-shift logic uses `speed`, fine.

One more thing: at very high speed in a curve, required lateral accel is huge; lateralV accumulates quickly, and the wall hit is inevitable even with braking if entering too fast. Good.

Add `shiftBlip` maybe no.

Apply resistance when clutch pressed: also applies lateral drift? `applyResistance` currently updates lateral with no curvature. Add stop drift.

Let me make the edit.

