      // smoke
```
Need:
```
const s = this.startS + sim.distance;
const f = this.track.frameAt(s);
const bank = clamp(f.kappa * sim.speed * sim.speed * 0.0045, -0.1, 0.1);
this.track.placeAt(this.playerGroup, s, this.track.LANE + sim.lateral, bank);
...
if (p.steeringWheel) { p.steeringWheel.rotation.z = this.steer*1.0; }
if (p.driver) {
  if (sim.gear !== this._gearShown) { this._gearShown = sim.gear; p.setGear?.(sim.gear); if (sim.gear !== 1 || this.mode === "race") p.driver.shift?.(); }
  p.driver.update(rdt, {steer:this.steer, time:this.time, speed:sim.speed});
}
```
Careful: on initial reset gear changes to 1; calling shift() moves hand oddly at race start. Only shift if mode race and gear changed after start. Track previous with `this._gearShown`. Set _gearShown=0 at startRace so first gear 1 triggers shift (drive gear). That's actually nice. In menu reset updates gear to 1; triggering hand to shifter in menu is okay but maybe weird. Limit to mode==="race".

Call `p.setGear(sim.gear)` always when changed.

Also driver.update needs called after wheel rotation. Yes.

Crash shake decay in frame: `this.crashShake = Math.max(0, (this.crashShake||0) - rdt*2.2)`.

Smoke: use rear wheels; positions world via getWorldPosition; good.

Rival placement with bank & kappa.

Also brake lights traverse uses emissive red; fine.

Let me patch.

