Now updateHud and telemetry finish. Let's patch telemetry:
```
finish: FINISH → finish: this.finishDistance
```
updateHud:
```
this.ui.setDist(sim.distance);
... setGap(... FINISH)
```
Add race line update throttled.

Also `ui.setGear(sim.gear, hint, sim.rpmNorm)` remains (gear moved to wheel in HTML).

Add after setGap:
```
this.lineAcc = (this.lineAcc||0) + ... but updateHud doesn't get rdt. Add rdt parameter? Called from frame: this.updateHud(); change to this.updateHud(rdt).
```
Use `this.time` compared to `this.lineClock` (0.12s).
```
if (this.mode === "race" && this.time - this.lineClock > 0.12) {
  this.lineClock = this.time;
  const sWorld = this.startS + sim.distance;
  const target = this.track.speedAt(sWorld);
  const ahead = this.track.stateAt(sWorld + 8);
  const corner = this.track.nextCorner(sWorld);
  let advice = "MANTÉM";
  if (sim.speed > target + 2.2) advice = "FREIA";
  else if (sim.speed < target - 3 && ahead === 2) advice = "ACELERA";
  else if (ahead === 2) advice = "ACELERA";
  this.ui.setRaceLine({
    advice, speed: sim.speedKmh,
    target: target * 3.6,
    cornerDist: corner ? Math.max(0, corner.entry - sWorld) : null,
    cornerDir: corner ? corner.dir : 0,
    cornerSpeed: corner ? corner.speed * 3.6 : null,
    profile: this.track.raceLine,
  });
}
```
For strip colors we need upcoming profile: UI can compute using states/profile/ds and startS+distance. Pass `profile`, `states`, `ds`, `sWorld`, `finishS`. The UI builds 26 segments:
```
const step = 12; const n=26; for i: s=sWorld+i*step; idx; color by state; except if beyond finish then dim.
```
We'll implement in ui.js `setRaceLine(state)`.

HUD callback each 0.12s fine.

Update timing: `this.lineClock` initialized 0 in initTrack.

Also set "FREIA" panel visible only race; maybe hide in menu: HUD only visible during race.

Patch updateHud signature and calls. In frame: `this.updateHud();` → `this.updateHud(rdt);` (rdt unused in method but pass maybe). Actually we use this.time, no rdt needed. Keep no args.

Let me patch.

